SUMMARY:Earth Day: Inuit Soap Carving Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Earth Day with through a hands-on workshop led by Inuk artist\, Barry Best\, combining storytelling\, creativity and reflection. \nPartners in Project Green members (including TRCA staff) are eligible for a discount. Contact charlotte.hung@trca.ca \nGET TICKETS \n– Explore Inuit values such as interconnectedness\, observation\, and respect for materials– Build cultural awareness through storytelling and shared creative experience– Discover The Village at Black Creek on a guided walk featuring artist Barry Best’s installation– Take home a sustainable\, hand-carved soap art piece you create yourself \nAccessibility accommodation: If you require accessibility accommodation\, please contact charlotte.hung@trca.ca.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/earth-day-inuit-soap-carving-workshop/
LOCATION:The Village at Black Creek\, 1000 Murray Ross Pkwy\, North York\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M3J 2P3
CATEGORIES:Art & Design,Classes & Workshops,Indigenous
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/earth-day-inuit-soap-carving-workshop.png
END:VEVENT
